{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrvXjc8nshUQYYQ5zXMs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `--json` to `wc` and the test suite passes (3 tests, including the existing text-output test).\n\nThe change is in `wc/cli.py`. With `--json`, each file's result is collected, and one JSON object is printed at the end with `files` and `total`. Without the flag, the per-file print and the multi-file `total` line run exactly as before, so text output should be unchanged. A missing file still prints its error to stderr and sets exit code 1, and in JSON mode it is left out of `files` and `total`.\n\nI added two tests in `tests/test_cli.py`: one for a single file, and one for several files where one is missing. The missing-file test checks the exit code, the `files` list, the totals, and the stderr message.\n\nTwo things to know:\n- `pytest` wasn't installed for the system Python, so I installed it with `pip install --user pytest`.\n- I did not commit. The changes are in the working tree."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10866,"cache_read_input_tokens":37180,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10866},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e4e82da-cbe0-4fd0-a9a1-e375f5195182","uuid":"75d4d4b4-587e-4160-b2f1-db5d1ac1d850","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:46:33.700Z","request_id":"req_011CfrvXjM1RoMzy9s26cLFV"}
